Rosalind, Callenbach completed floor flatness and levelness testing on the =
level two operations hall slab last Wednesday, within 24 hours of finishing=
 as the specification requires. Composite readings came in at FF 28 and FL =
22 against a specified FF 35 and FL 25, with two bays in the northeast quad=
rant well below that.<br />
<br />
For a raised access floor this matters less than it would for sheet goods, =
but the pedestal heights in those two bays will need shimming beyond the ma=
nufacturer's standard adjustment range. My recommendation is grinding the h=
igh spots and a self leveling underlayment in the two failing bays before t=
he pedestal layout starts.